<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Sola urges beef offensive against U.S.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Sola urges beef offensive against U.S.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine beef producers must be ready to fight in international markets against United States output, Agriculture Secretary Felipe Sola said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The United States is going to try and flood the international market in the process of liquidating stocks. Our country can and must win this battle,&quot; said Sola, speaking at a seminar in the beachside town of Mar del Plata.</p>
<p>Saying Argentina would be officially declared free of foot and mouth disease in 1997, Sola called for marketing campaigns to promote Argentine beef abroad. He proposed the creation of a fund to finance beef promotion.</p>
<p>-- Jason webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
